module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.GysinCartierIntersection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.CartierRegular.FrameTrivialization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.LocalEquationJet
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth.FibreRegularity
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth.HypersurfaceStalkRegular
public import StacksFrontier.FieldTheory.Separable.PerfectField

/-!
# The Jacobian criterion for the zero scheme of a section of an invertible module

Let `ℒ` be an invertible module on a scheme `X`, let `s` be a section of `ℒ` and let
`Z = Z(s)` be its zero scheme. At a point `z` of `Z` lying over `y ∈ X`, if the local ring
`𝒪_{X,y}` is regular and the germ of `s` at `y` does **not** lie in `𝔪_y²ℒ_y`, then the local
ring `𝒪_{Z,z}` is regular.

This is the Jacobian criterion in the form the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] uses it: there the
condition `s_y ∉ 𝔪_y²ℒ_y` is exactly the non-vanishing of the evaluation `ev_y` of the linear
system at the vector cutting out the divisor, and the conclusion feeds the characterisation of
smoothness of a fibre by regularity of its local rings.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul`: **the stalk
  of `Z(s)` at a point where `s` does not vanish to second order is a regular local ring**, when
  the ambient stalk is.

## Implementation notes

Three facts are combined, and the whole content of this file is that they can be combined: the
ideal of `Z(s)` in the stalk is principal, generated by the local equation of `s` read through a
trivialization (`Stacks.Chow.ker_zeroScheme_stalkMap_of_frame`); that generator lies in `𝔪_y`
(`Stacks.Chow.frame_coordinate_mem_maximalIdeal`); and it avoids `𝔪_y²` exactly when the germ of
`s` avoids `𝔪_y²ℒ_y` (`Stacks.LocalEquationJet.Γgerm_mem_maximalSqSmul_iff`). The quotient of a
regular local ring by such an element is regular
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_ker_stalkMap_eq_span_singleton`).

The first two facts are stated for a trivialization written as an isomorphism `ℒ|_U ≅ 𝒪_U` and
the third for a `Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization`; the two are the same datum, by
`Stacks.Divisors.frameTrivialization`, whose trivializing map over `U` is
`Stacks.Divisors.frameSections` on the nose. That identification is what lets a single affine
open serve both.

The section is taken as a `PresheafOfModules.sections` rather than as an element of `Γ(ℒ, ⊤)`,
matching `Stacks.Chow.ker_zeroScheme_stalkMap_of_frame`; the two are interchangeable by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTopOfRingSheaf`, whose value over `⊤` is the given element.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is a step inside the proof of Tag 0FD6.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FD6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FD6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory IsLocalRing TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open Stacks.Chow Stacks.Divisors Stacks.LocalEquationJet
open Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules)
  [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]

/-- **The Jacobian criterion for a zero scheme.** Let `ℒ` be an invertible module on `X`, let
`s` be a section of `ℒ`, and let `z` be a point of the zero scheme `Z(s)` lying over `y ∈ X`.
If `𝒪_{X,y}` is a regular local ring and the germ of `s` at `y` does not lie in `𝔪_y²ℒ_y`, then
`𝒪_{Z(s),z}` is a regular local ring.

The ideal of `Z(s)` in `𝒪_{X,y}` is generated by the local equation of `s` at `y`, which lies in
`𝔪_y` because `s` vanishes at `y`, and avoids `𝔪_y²` exactly because the germ of `s` avoids
`𝔪_y²ℒ_y`; the quotient of a regular local ring by such an element is regular. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_stalk_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul (s : L.sections)
    (z : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme)
    [IsRegularLocalRing
      (X.presheaf.stalk ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))]
    (hs : (L.presheaf.Γgerm ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)).hom
        (s.eval (op ⊤)) ∉
      maximalSqSmul L ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)) :
    IsRegularLocalRing ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.presheaf.stalk z) := by
  set y := (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z with hy
  obtain ⟨U, eU, -, hyU, -⟩ := exists_affine_frame_subset X L y ⊤ trivial
  set a : Γ(X, U.1) := frameSections X L eU
    (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op (s.eval (op ⊤))) with ha
  have hrange : y ∈ Set.range (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι :=
    Set.mem_range_self z
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι] at hrange
  have hsupp : y ∈ (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).support := hrange
  have hmem : (X.presheaf.germ U.1 y hyU).hom a ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y) :=
    frame_coordinate_mem_maximalIdeal X L s U eU y hyU hsupp
  have hker : RingHom.ker
      ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι.stalkMap z).hom =
      Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U.1 y hyU).hom a} :=
    ker_zeroScheme_stalkMap_of_frame X L s U eU z hyU
  have hnot : (X.presheaf.germ U.1 y hyU).hom a ∉ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2 :=
    fun h => hs ((Γgerm_mem_maximalSqSmul_iff (frameTrivialization eU) hyU
      (s.eval (op ⊤))).mpr h)
  exact isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_ker_stalkMap_eq_span_singleton _ z hmem hnot hker

/-- **The Jacobian criterion over a field.** Let `ℒ` be an invertible module on a scheme `X`,
let `s` be a section of `ℒ` and let `Z(s)` be its zero scheme, a scheme locally of finite type
over a field `k`. At a point `z` of `Z(s)` lying over `y ∈ X` with `𝒪_{X,y}` regular, whose
residue field is separable over `k`, the divisor `Z(s)` is smooth over `k` as soon as the germ
of `s` at `y` does not lie in `𝔪_y²ℒ_y`.

This is the form in which the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] uses the criterion: the hypothesis on
the germ is exactly the non-vanishing of the evaluation `ev_y` of the linear system at the
vector cutting out the divisor, and at a closed point over an algebraically closed field the
separability condition is vacuous. -/
theorem smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul {k : Type u} [Field k] (s : L.sections)
    (g : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType g]
    (z : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme)
    [IsRegularLocalRing
      (X.presheaf.stalk ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))]
    (hs : (L.presheaf.Γgerm ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)).hom
        (s.eval (op ⊤)) ∉
      maximalSqSmul L ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))
    (hsep : letI : Algebra k ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.residueField z) :=
        ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ g.appTop ≫
          (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.Γevaluation z).hom.toAlgebra
      Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k
        ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.residueField z)) :
    InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt g z :=
  (smoothAt_iff_isRegularLocalRing_stalk g z hsep).mpr
    (isRegularLocalRing_stalk_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul L s z hs)

/-- **The Jacobian criterion over a perfect field**, with no separability side condition: over a
perfect field every residue field extension is separable
(`Algebra.isSeparableExtension_of_perfectField`). This is the situation of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0FD6] after the base field has been enlarged to an algebraic closure, an
algebraically closed field being perfect.

Perfection is what the separability side condition of
`AlgebraicGeometry.smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul` costs, and it is the whole cost:
nothing below uses roots of inseparable polynomials. It cannot be weakened to separable
closedness, which does not imply it — over a separably closed `k` of characteristic `p` with
`a ∈ k ∖ k^p` the section `T^p - a` of `𝒪` on the smooth `k`-scheme `𝔸¹` satisfies the germ
hypothesis, and its zero scheme `Spec k(a^{1/p})` is regular but not smooth over `k`. -/
theorem smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul_of_perfectField {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [PerfectField k] (s : L.sections)
    (g : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType g]
    (z : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme)
    [IsRegularLocalRing
      (X.presheaf.stalk ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))]
    (hs : (L.presheaf.Γgerm ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)).hom
        (s.eval (op ⊤)) ∉
      maximalSqSmul L ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)) :
    InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt g z := by
  let : Algebra k ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.residueField z) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ g.appTop ≫
      (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme.Γevaluation z).hom.toAlgebra
  exact smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul L s g z hs
    (Algebra.isSeparableExtension_of_perfectField k _)

/-- **The Jacobian criterion over an algebraically closed field**, with no separability side
condition: over a perfect field every residue field extension is separable, and an
algebraically closed field is perfect. This is the situation of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0FD6] after the base field has been enlarged. -/
theorem smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul_of_isAlgClosed {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] (s : L.sections)
    (g : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType g]
    (z : (zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme)
    [IsRegularLocalRing
      (X.presheaf.stalk ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))]
    (hs : (L.presheaf.Γgerm ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)).hom
        (s.eval (op ⊤)) ∉
      maximalSqSmul L ((zeroScheme X L (s.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)) :
    InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt g z :=
  smoothAt_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul_of_perfectField L s g z hs

/-- **Regularity of a local ring travels along an isomorphism of schemes.** The stalk map of an
isomorphism at a point is an isomorphism of rings. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_iso {A B : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (z : A)
    [IsRegularLocalRing (A.presheaf.stalk z)] :
    IsRegularLocalRing (B.presheaf.stalk (e.hom.base z)) :=
  IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv
    (asIso (e.hom.stalkMap z)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- **A flat morphism is smooth at a point of a fibre which is a divisor not vanishing to second
order there.** Let `g : Y ⟶ S` be flat and locally of finite presentation and let the fibre of
`g` over `s` be identified with the zero scheme `Z(σ)` of a section of an invertible module on a
scheme `X`. At a point `z` of `Z(σ)` lying over a point of `X` with regular local ring, at which
the germ of `σ` avoids `𝔪²ℒ` and whose residue field is separable over `κ(s)`, the morphism `g`
is smooth.

This is the passage from the divisor `H_a` to the morphism `q` of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0FD6]: the identification of the fibre is supplied by the cartesian square
presenting `H_a` as a fibre of `q`, and the hypothesis on the germ is the non-vanishing of the
evaluation of the linear system. -/
theorem smoothAt_fiberι_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul {Y S : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ S) [Flat g]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation g] (s : S) (σ : L.sections)
    (e : (zeroScheme X L (σ.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme ≅ g.fiber s)
    (z : (zeroScheme X L (σ.eval (op ⊤))).subscheme)
    [IsRegularLocalRing
      (X.presheaf.stalk ((zeroScheme X L (σ.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))]
    (hσ : (L.presheaf.Γgerm ((zeroScheme X L (σ.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z)).hom
        (σ.eval (op ⊤)) ∉
      maximalSqSmul L ((zeroScheme X L (σ.eval (op ⊤))).subschemeι z))
    (hsep : letI : Algebra (S.residueField s) ((g.fiber s).residueField (e.hom.base z)) :=
        ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (S.residueField s)).inv ≫
          (g.fiberToSpecResidueField s).appTop ≫
            (g.fiber s).Γevaluation (e.hom.base z)).hom.toAlgebra
      Algebra.IsSeparableExtension (S.residueField s)
        ((g.fiber s).residueField (e.hom.base z))) :
    InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt g (g.fiberι s (e.hom.base z)) :=
  have := isRegularLocalRing_stalk_zeroScheme_of_notMem_maximalSqSmul L σ z hσ
  smoothAt_fiberι_of_isRegularLocalRing_stalk g s (e.hom.base z)
    (isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_iso e z) hsep

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
